<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<page>
  <title>DevAlert Backend Settings using AWS</title>
  <keywords>
    <keyword>amazon</keyword>
    <keyword>web</keyword>
    <keyword>services</keyword>
    <keyword>aws</keyword>
    <keyword>dev</keyword>
    <keyword>alert</keyword>
    <keyword>devalert</keyword>
    <keyword>cloud</keyword>
    <keyword>trace</keyword>
  </keywords>
  <body>
    <section>
      <header>Overview</header>
      <text>
        <p>
          The settings here are for connecting from $PNAME to your AWS cloud account,
          to be able to retrieve the traces.
        </p>

        <p>
          <A HREF="img/DevAlert_Storage_Settings_AWS.png" target="$IMAGETARGET">
            <img src="img/DevAlert_Storage_Settings_AWS.png" width="$IMAGEWIDTH" border="0" />
          </A>
        </p>

        <subsection>
          <header>AWS Profile</header>
          <text>
            <p>
              An AWS profile must be set up with information from your AWS administrator.
            </p>
          </text>
        </subsection>
        <subsection>
          <header>Settings</header>
          <text>
            <p>
              When DevAlert is setup, a settings file is generated by the AWS administrator
              who set up the storage. This file can be imported by using <b>Import AWS Settings</b>
              from the bottom and browse for the file.
            </p>
            <p>
              The <b>Test</b> button will verify the Profile, Region and Role ARN (if set).
            </p>
          </text>
        </subsection>
      </text>
    </section>
  </body>
</page>